; VU1 microprogram (generated by tools/vu1/gen.py mapi, do not edit): indexed map chunks (shared vertices: each vertex
; is sent and transformed once, like the shared-vertex data of Sony's HiG and other indexed PS2 renderers), software
; pipelined. Input: header 0-6 as vu1map2.vsm (0 {tris, cull mask, st scale K, edge fog slope a2}, 1 {origin xyz,
; step}, 2 A+D GIF tag, 3-5 TEX0 / TEX1 / TEST, 6 PRIM tag with NLOOP 3 + EOP), 7 {vertex passes = vertices / 3,
; offset of the triangle stream from the batch start, 0, 0}; vertices at 8, 3 qw each (s16 pos, u16 st, u8 colour;
; the exporter pads the count to a multiple of 3); then one qword per triangle: u8 x4 {v0, v1, v2, 0} (vertex
; numbers). Constants as vu1map2.vsm.
; Pass 1, three vertices per loop pass, in place: vu1map2's vertex math (view, fog, the edge fog in a second loop taken
; as in vu1map2, CLIP, q, STQ, screen); qword 0 <- XYZF2 (ftoi4 screen, fog), 1 <- STQ with .w = 1 when the vertex is
; outside a clip plane, 2 (colour) kept.
; Pass 2, one loop pass per triangle: its three vertices are copied into output slot VI08 (994 / 1004,
; alternating, shared with vu1map2 / vu1clip) as one GIF packet; ADC on the third vertex when a vertex is flagged or
; the cull mask catches the screen cross product, as in vu1map2.

; pass 1: 72 cycles per 3 vertices (edge fog loop 84), pass 2: 49 cycles per triangle in the tools/vu1 timing model

		.vu
		.align 4
		.global VU1MapI_CodeStart
		.global VU1MapI_CodeEnd
VU1MapI_CodeStart:
	NOP                            	lq VF01,0(VI00)
